{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/763367-3e-homebrew-lightbringers-an-alternate-solar-creation-advancement-system-3e-update","id":763367,"title":"[3E Homebrew]Lightbringers: An alternate Solar creation/advancement system, 3E update","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-11T12:51:18-08:00","id":763367,"title":"[3E Homebrew]Lightbringers: An alternate Solar creation/advancement system, 3E update","content":"When I was doing my first ST for 2E, I stumbled upon <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?608889-Exalted-The-Lightbringers-Alternate-Solar-Creation-Advancement\" target=\"_blank\">Mengtzu\u2019s Lightbringers system</a>. It was pretty much exactly what I needed without even knowing that I wanted it: Simple, straightforward, easy to keep track of at all times (as this was my first campaign and there was a waiting list of players, the ability to swap new people in seamlessly following an accidental culling was glorious), and with an eye towards ensuring the play experience was fun for all levels of player knowledge.<br /> <br /> As I start brainstorming my first 3E campaign I\u2019ve decided to take a crack at updating Lightbringers for the new edition. Of course, I don\u2019t have anywhere near the skill or knowledge of Mengtzu, so I was hoping I could tap into some of the forum braintrust to help me out and point out any glaring errors.<br /> <br /> The following is a proposed Lightbringer setup for 3E. I\u2019ve spoilered my thoughts and concerns at the very bottom.<br /> <br /> This package of house rules has a number of related goals:<br /> - Providing a structure for relatively short campaigns (less than a year of weekly sessions).<br /> - Supporting a mode of play in which all PCs participate equally in combat and non-combat scenes.<br /> - Providing rapid advancement that nonetheless has a sensible learning curve.<br /> - Improving balance between PCs at the table, both to make the game friendlier to new or less system-expert players, and to make it easier for the ST to provide appropriate challenges.<br /> <br /> These house-rules should be used in proportion to how useful you find these goals.<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">-Character Creation-</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Caste</b> \u2013 Choose as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Circle Goals -</b> The group should decide together on a mutual goal for the Circle that will form the backbone of the first ~10 sessions of play. This should be at the national/regional level and pose a good challenge for Essence 1 characters.<br /> <br /> <b>Character Goals</b> \u2013 Each character\u2019s individual goals should be on a national/regional level achievable within a relatively short time-frame (think \u201clocal epic\u201d). Each Player should have a Defining Intimacy related to that goal, whether a general Principle or Tie to someone/something associated with it. Players wanting a Creation-spanning goal should choose an achievable subset and upgrade as the campaign progresses. Personal goals should be compatible with that of the Circle (dramatic tension is good, having no reason to work with the Circle is bad).<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b><br /> - All attributes begin with one dot.<br /> - Set Dexterity to 5.<br /> - Choose one Social and one Mental attribute to be rated at 5.<br /> - Distribute 6 points in your primary category, 4 in your secondary, 2 in your tertiary.<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b><br /> 1. Choose a Supernal Ability to be rated at 5. If your chosen Supernal Ability is one of the choices listed in step 2 or 3, you may skip that step and instead choose an additional ability, for a total of 3, during step 5.<br /> 2. Choose one of Archery, Brawl, Martial Arts* (any subset), Melee, and Thrown to be rated at 5.<br /> 3. Choose one of Integrity, Presence, Performance, Investigation, and Socialize to be rated at 5.<br /> 4. Choose three of your Caste abilities to be rated at 5.<br /> 5. Choose any two other abilities to be rated at 5. If you do not have Brawl, Martial Arts or Melee rated at 5, you must ensure that Dodge or Resistance is amongst your abilities rated at 5.<br /> 6. Distribute 12 points amongst the remaining abilities, no more than 3 points to any one ability.<br /> 7. Craft* is a single ability for Lightbringers.<br /> 8. Choose a specialty for each ability rated at 5.<br /> <br /> <i>*Craft</i> - Craft is a single ability to the Lightbringers - their understanding of one field translates effortlessly to another. However specialized supernatural crafts require an appropriate specialty, or the crafter suffers a -2 internal penalty. Obtaining such a specialty requires an in-character justification, but not a particularly robust one - transcendent skill doesn\u2019t require much to go on.<br /> <br /> *<i>Martial Arts</i> \u2013 Lightbringers do not need to purchase any additional Merits to get dots in a Martial Arts style. They must still obtain dots in each style separately.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b><br /> - Gain Artifact 5. This must be distributed between artifacts with a rating no greater than 3, ideally weapons and armor. This represents spoils from unsuccessful Wyld Hunts, past life tomb raiding, gifts from mysterious benefactors, etc.<br /> - Distribute 10 points amongst other Merits, except Manse.<br /> <br /> NOTE: For Lightbringers, change the text of the Martial Arts Merit to the following<br /> Martial Arts (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) Purchased - The character had a innate understanding of the underlying values of the martial arts before being Exalted; The awakening of her Essence has only caused that familiarity to blossom. Treat the character\u2019s Essence as one dot higher for the purpose of purchasing Martial Arts Charms.<br /> <br /> <b>Charms</b><br /> -Choose 5 Charms useful in martial combat.<br /> -Choose 5 Charms useful in social or non-combat scenes<br /> -Choose 5 additional Charms of any type.<br /> -Spells may be substituted for charms according to their function (ie Flying Guillotine may replace a combat charm choice, Infallible Messenger a non-combat choice, Summon Elemental either, etc.).<br /> <br /> <b>Finishing Touches:</b><br /> - All Lightbringers start with Essence 1.<br /> - All Lightbringers start with Willpower 6.<br /> - Calculate essence pools as normal.<br /> - Gain Health Levels as normal.<br /> - Lightbringers do not receive bonus points.<br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>-Advancement and Campaign Structure-</b></span></u><br /> A Lightbringers campaign is intended to run over arcs of ten sessions each, up to five times (for a total of 50 sessions). Character advancement does not occur with XP, but on a schedule over the course of these sessions.<br /> <br /> All PCs are always at an identical state of advancement. No character is deprived advancement if their player missed a session, nor can any bonuses be earned. If a new player joins, or an old character needs to be replaced, the new character joins at the same state of advancement as the rest. This not only naturally preserves balance, but explicitly distinguishes character advancement from reward - new charms are not a privilege awarded for good play, but a periodic milestone in the player\u2019s learning curve.<br /> <br /> <b>Campaign Arcs</b><br /> Each arc is intended to last ten sessions, allowing a five-arc campaign of weekly sessions to fit comfortably in a calendar year of real time.<br /> <br /> Each arc deals primarily with the Circle\u2019s shared Goal. That Goal should be resolved - by success, failure or perhaps a dramatic change in the Circle\u2019s perspective - by the end of the arc. As a result sessions should be fairly focused and fast-paced, with some sort of decisive change to the local status quo by session end, in order to build steadily towards the arc\u2019s climax. That doesn\u2019t mean the arc or sessions should be linear - just that even in pure sandbox mode with the PCs striking out wherever interests them, something should happen as a result.<br /> <br /> Once the arc is finished, the group should assess the story and then choose a new or evolved Circle Goal that represents an escalation over the one just resolved (this is also a good time to re-examine personal goals and Intimacies, as they were hopefully a big part of the arc themselves).<br /> <br /> Sample Arc Progression<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Sakuya, Reimu, Marisa, Arisu and Sanae are a Circle of Lightbringers arising in the Dreaming Sea. Their first Circle Goal is to win a Sea-wide race presided over by Mercury herself, building up their ship while sabotaging others. After winning the race, for Arc 2 they take their prize, a treasure map leading to the hoard of a First Age Pirate Exigent, all the while dodging the enemies and rivals made during the race, as well as the Sidereals and Abyssals who have designs on the treasure. Upon finding the hoard, they discover that it was actually a prison for an unstuck in time Balor, who is released during an epic battle. For Arc 3 they must unite the warring Prasad, Volivat, and Ysyr to combat a brewing Second Balorian Crusade. After repelling the Fair Folk, the next Arc finds the Circle then setting out to formalize their new Dreaming Sea Confederation, overcoming centuries of hatred just in time for a two pronged attack from The Realm and Ixcoatli. During the war the portal to Zen Mu is opened after an errant shot from the Realm Defense Grid, and during Arc 5 the Circle must find a way to stop or control the portal's inhabitants from wreaking mass havoc and destruction.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Advancement during the Arc</b><br /> -At the end of every session, each character receives one charm. The group together decides whether combat or non-combat was the most decisive arena in the last two sessions (ie whether they used their combat or non-combat charms more). The charm gained is of that type. Alternately, groups wishing to avoid a positive feedback loop can make the gained charm of the opposite type, creating an incentive to bounce back and forth between violent and non-violent solutions to your problems as you gain new charms.<br /> -At the end of every odd session of an arc (eg 1st, 3rd, 5th etc), each character receives 1 ability dot to assign as they please. They may exchange this instead for two specialties. This generally should have some fictional justification, even if it\u2019s just a note of the character taking an interest in the ability during downtime.<br /> -At the end of every even session of an arc (eg 2<sup>nd</sup>, 4<sup>th</sup>, 6<sup>th</sup>, etc.) each character receives a Martial Arts charm, spell, Evocation, or (if Eclipse) spirit Charm they qualify for. If the character has no such Charms they want or qualify for, they may instead gain 3 dots of Merits (usually these will be Purchased Merits only, although the ST may allow some Story Merits to be purchased this way at their discretion).<br /> -At the end of every fifth session, add 10 XP to a pool shared by the group. This XP may be spent by the group on anything that has an XP cost, such as sorcerous workings, familiar training, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Advancement at the end of an Arc</b><br /> At the end of an arc, each character gains:<br /> - 1 Attribute dot<br /> - 1 dot of Essence<br /> - 1 dot of Willpower<br /> - 1 new Defining Intimacy (whether completely new as a result of the arc or an existing Intimacy increased in strength)<br /> This should be accompanied by some downtime narration of how their experiences have caused them to grow as an Exalt and a person (particularly the double-edged sword of a new Defining Intimacy).<br /> <br /> <b>Gaining Merits</b><br /> Story Merits should be very easy to acquire in play, to the extent there are no rules for them (save for the exception covered above for every odd session of an arc). Players should naturally assume that easy come means easy go.<br /> <br /> Manses are a somewhat more difficult case, and players should assume they are both harder to obtain and less likely to be taken away by the winds of fate. However the ST should allow every reasonable opportunity to gain possession of Manses in play.<br /> <br /> <b>Gaining Artifacts and Evocations</b><br /> Artifacts can be gained organically in play by normal means - seeking out First Age ruins, taking them from the bodies of foes, or crafting.<br /> <br /> However, once the Lightbringers have established their mark on the world, their artifacts will begin to thrum alongside their wielder\u2019s legend. During the downtime between the first and second campaign arc, each character\u2019s artifacts begin to develop free Evocations that apply benefits upon attuning. The player may narrate how these Evocations arose however they please (e.g. from the weapon gaining further sentience, the lingering effects of a defeated foe, blessings from a powerful spirit, etc.). Characters that do not use weapons or armor (generally martial artists) should negotiate with the ST an appropriate substitute useful in combat.<br /> <br /> Every third session thereafter, each character comes into possession of a miscellaneous artifact or hearthstone with a rating equal to the character\u2019s essence. Most such artifacts should be of non-combat utility. The ST and player should work together for the appearance of these artifacts making sense in the fiction, including breaking the regular three-session schedule when needed (so long as it works out roughly equivalent over time).<br /> <br /> In the downtime at the end of arcs 3 and 4, each character\u2019s weapon and armor are upgraded to have an artifact rating equal to the character\u2019s Essence (4 and 5 respectively) with the potential for Evocations to match. This may entail discovering a new panoply and setting the old gear aside, the gods of the artifacts receiving well-deserved promotions and unlocking more of their ancient power thereby, or the discovery that their \u2018mere\u2019 daiklave is in actuality the Volcano Cutter of legend.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcs of irregular length</b><br /> Campaigns tend to find their own length, and resist planning. It\u2019s fine for an arc to take as long as makes sense for your table (and in particular much longer if your group prefers to climb the Essence tiers more slowly and has time).<br /> <br /> <b>Rebuilding</b><br /> Players should be allowed to rebuild their characters between sessions within reason. Enjoyment of the character and opportunity to exercise a deeper understanding of the system outweigh any minor continuity problems. No character should be haunted by an unwise charm selection for their entire career.<br /> <br /> However Solar Exalted are not Alchemical Exalted; such changes should be for the purpose of becoming more comfortable with the character, not adapting to local tactical conditions. Furthermore, particularly radical changes such as changing caste or retconning the entire character concept will not seem appropriate to most groups. In such cases it\u2019s probably better to retire the character and create a new one.<br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>-What does this mean?-</b></span></u><br /> All Lightbringers start with very high attack and defence dice pools and 5 combat charms. The whole Circle are first-class citizens in action scenes.<br /> <br /> All Lightbringers start with a strong mortal-level package for social combat, and 5 non-combat charms. The whole Circle are first-class citizens in non-combat scenes.<br /> <br /> Optimised mortal dice pools is something a Lightbringer Circle gets for free. Their strategy and growth is intended to be almost entirely in the realm of Charms.<br /> <br /> The cost is in flexibility. Without bonus points, many mechanical character arrangements become impossible, and the specific structures used above prevent some valid builds (such as having all Caste abilities rated at 5). While most of these expressions are suboptimal and not appropriate for a balance-focused campaign, the group/ST should be open to moving around ability and attribute points somewhat to better fit a concept.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Circle and Character Goals<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The original Lightbringers referred to 2E\u2019s Motivation, the system term. I switched that out to goal, just the simple noun. Even though it has no system meaning, I still think it\u2019s a good idea for players/the group to consider going in. Requiring a Defining Intimacy seems like the closest I can get to the original Motivation concept.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Attributes<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Unchanged from original Lightbringers. Dex might not be the god stat it once was, but it\u2019s still the Prince of Earth of attributes. Setting it to 5 is also useful for maintaining the optimized fighting pool.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Abilities<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Addition of Supernal is a simple update. Lightbringer wrinkles for MA and Craft are covered later, hence the asterisks. Not sure if I worded step 1 super clearly; Trying to avoid a situation where, say, Supernal Melee is chosen first and then the player thinks they have to add another combat ability at 5 even if they are fine with just Melee. The original rules allowed three specialties for each ability rated at 5, thought that might have been overkill with the new 3E specialty rules.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Craft<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This was the original rule hack. I <i>think</i> it still works for 3E, although it would require shooing a player away from any Craft charms that worked on switching Craft dots around. It\u2019s also possible that this is the worst mistake ever with horrible knock on effects.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Martial Arts<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The elimination of the Merit will probably be relatively uncontroversial. Having one MA skill to cover all styles still feels too strong, so buying them separately is kept in. Again, this feels like something that feels ok but might be catastrophic/overpowered in practice.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Merits<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Artifact rules in the original Lightbringers were oriented around Jade artifacts, when each MM had different stats. Now that stats are standardized it probably doesn\u2019t matter the Artifact\u2019s composition. Since the Martial Arts Merit is no longer necessary just to get MA dots, I tried to spice up the Merit for Lightbringers.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Charms<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The original Lightbringers made sure that every character had at least a perfect defense. That\u2019s not really necessary in 3E, but I kept the minimums for in and out of combat Charms. I thought about giving 10 Charms of any type, but choosing 20 Charms at chargen might be pushing it.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Finishing Touches<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Original Lightbringers started at Essence 2, because that\u2019s what chargen Essence was in 2E, and Willpower 7. I lowered it to Willpower 6 because my Lightbringers campaigns envision an additional arc.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Advancements During the Arc<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This is by far the biggest divergence from the old Lightbringers, where a Charm was given out only at the end of the even sessions. However, due to the much expanded library of Charms in 3E and the increased focus on combining multiple Charms rather than obtaining and mastering fire and forget Charms, I think it justifies increasing the player\u2019s Charm intake?? From my back of the envelope math, if you spent regular XP just on favored charms you\u2019d end up purchasing ~ 37 Charms when you reached Essence 5 by RAW, whereas here you\u2019ll have 40. Of course, you\u2019ll also be doing that in 40 sessions here compared to 60 sessions by RAW\u2026<br /> <br /> The odd session/ability dot section hasn\u2019t changed. The even session charms are intended to reflect expenditures of Solar XP, with the Merit rider due to the fact that if you aren\u2019t a MA/sorcery/Evocation user you shouldn\u2019t be punished. Might need to clarify the Story Merit aside some; Intention is that the player may want to get, say, Contacts or Resources, but not have the justification for it currently in the campaign. By negotiating with the ST to \u2018purchase\u2019 the Merit the ST agrees to fudge or add a situation to the campaign to accommodate acquiring the Merit for the player.<br /> <br /> The pool of community XP is to cover the fact that there are a few more sources of XP cost requirements this edition, while Lightbringers envisions XP-less play. Not sure if that amount should be upped a bit, maybe to 15-20 XP every five sessions, since the pool has to cover everyone.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Advancement at the End of an Arc<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This is mostly from the original Lightbringers, although I swapped out a new Virtue dot for a new Defining Intimacy. That seems like a crude approximation, and I think I might just axe the new intimacy stuff.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> Gaining Artifacts and Evocations<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">This section in the original Lightbringers was very focused on upgrading the jade chargen artifacts to orichalcum, as MM mattered a great deal in 2E. In 3E, with its standardized weapon stats, I\u2019ve tried to keep the same feel of an upgraded panoply with free natural/attuned Evocations. It\u2019ll probably take until Arms of the Chosen is released before this won\u2019t require homebrewing, but seeing as they don\u2019t start appearing until 10 sessions in hopefully the players and ST will be comfortable enough to come up with their own.<br /> <br /> Another thought I had was just giving the character\u2019s artifacts uniform stat/number upgrades, like additional accuracy dice or Hardness, to convey that even among artifacts the Lightbringers have something special.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The last two sections are unchanged from original flavor Lightbringers.<br /> <br /> The original system included some additional mechanical tweaks, but were mostly oriented around 2E concerns I don\u2019t think are present in 3E. The only ones I might consider bringing over unchanged is doubling base Strength for Feats of Strength purposes (but my perusal of 3E Athletics suggests that\u2019s not as necessary now) or the prospect of getting Stamina/2 as base Hardness that can stack with armor. Mengtzu also had some fun flavor bits and helpful tips on constructing arcs and campaigns that I might also just yoink and reproduce.<br /> <br /> For now though, I\u2019m just looking at the above and hoping I didn\u2019t miss something that\u2019ll cause it to fall apart when the rubber hits the road.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":870,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","user":"Side Item","date":". 11-11-2015, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T13:39:09-08:00","id":763408,"title":"","content":"This looks fantastic.<br /> <br /> Might have to rebuild some Craft charms like you did with the MA merit to preserve prereqs. But I'm tempted to use this forever and ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T15:11:42-08:00","id":763509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/763367-3e-homebrew-lightbringers-an-alternate-solar-creation-advancement-system-3e-update#post763367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Set Dexterity to 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without getting into the rest of it just now, I think you should consider just making it one physical attribute set to 5. Having a dex of less than 5 is no longer a death sentence. A Strength-focused character using Increasing Strength Exercise and Brawl Charms or a Stamina-focused Resistance Supernal are quite formidable.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Having read it more fully, I don't really like this. It seems to have been written with certain assumptions about play that I do not share. I don't particularly want to be told that I must take a combat ability at 5 and Artifact 5. I think Exalted in general and 3e in particular is designed with broader sensibilities in mind than hard balancing everyone for combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 11-11-2015, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T18:01:43-08:00","id":763626,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This looks fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Might have to rebuild some Craft charms like you did with the MA merit to preserve prereqs. But I'm tempted to use this forever and ever.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As I want to keep stressing, pretty much everything good is result of Mengtzu, I'm mostly just doodling mash notes to 3E in the margins.</span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Without getting into the rest of it just now, I think you should consider just making it one physical attribute set to 5. Having a dex of less than 5 is no longer a death sentence. A Strength-focused character using Increasing Strength Exercise and Brawl Charms or a Stamina-focused Resistance Supernal are quite formidable.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Having read it more fully, I don't really like this. It seems to have been written with certain assumptions about play that I do not share. I don't particularly want to be told that I must take a combat ability at 5 and Artifact 5. I think Exalted in general and 3e in particular is designed with broader sensibilities in mind than hard balancing everyone for combat.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It might be because I didn't include the original reasoning and goals of the system (which I'm working on working into the original post), but you're not wrong (although I don't think your criticisms are completely founded).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Lightbringers is intended for new players and is designed so that at all times each member of the party is capable of contributing to the action. So you get things like everyone having Dex 5 and a combat ability (so that everyone has at least mortal optimized pools in battle), but also required to have a 5 point social ability and Charms capable of helping outside of combat. Each member of the Circle can be confident that they can be proactive no matter where they can find themselves (&quot;Invincible Sword Princess and her squishy friends&quot; isn't a major problem in 3E</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Now, to accomplish this is does mean that certain builds are shut out. You can't go 15 Charms deep into your Supernal from chargen, you can't play the dedicated pacifist nor the monofocused combat beast, etc. That's the cost of making Circle-balance the overriding concern, but I see it as a feature not a bug. (Additionally, there was also a part in the original I haven't ported over yet that mentioned that switching around dots and fudging things for a given concept is possible, as long as it didn't result in something too suboptimal compared to the rest of the Circle.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In that vein, your point about how the Physical Attributes are now more even in the new edition is very true. The original said that Dex should never ever go below 5, but I think in the new edition if the player came to the ST and could petition as you did for opting out of Dex 5 and making either Stamina or Strength 5 instead that could be an option. However, I think it would require a bit of non-newbie system knowhow to realize those were reasonable builds to short Dex somewhat to obtain; Meanwhile, having Dex 5 never really hurts and is usually a great boon, so making it a mandatory opt-in for players is the simple option.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And finally, being honest, not sure what the exact problem with the Artifact requirement is? I always liked it for how it gave players fun toys right from the get go.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T23:57:50-08:00","id":763819,"title":"","content":"My issue with this for new players is that, while no one will have an ineffective character, character creation is a lot more intimidating in a way that could carry over into the game. It sends the message that 5s are necessary because the system is so brittle and because organic choices will ruin your character. Lightbringers helped in 2e, where it really did protect people from a lot of bad surprises.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want to make a player think, &quot;Oh shit, I've only got 7 dice in Charisma + Presence. I should shut up and let the good characters handle this,&quot; or &quot;My score isn't 5 in this ability, so picking up charms is a waste.&quot; Of course you can communicate to your players that they don't need huge dice pools to succeed or to invest in an area, but anyone willing to say that probably wouldn't use this system...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T00:38:22-08:00","id":763837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/763367-3e-homebrew-lightbringers-an-alternate-solar-creation-advancement-system-3e-update?p=763509#post763509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without getting into the rest of it just now, I think you should consider just making it one physical attribute set to 5. Having a dex of less than 5 is no longer a death sentence. A Strength-focused character using Increasing Strength Exercise and Brawl Charms or a Stamina-focused Resistance Supernal are quite formidable.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Having read it more fully, I don't really like this. It seems to have been written with certain assumptions about play that I do not share. I don't particularly want to be told that I must take a combat ability at 5 and Artifact 5. I think Exalted in general and 3e in particular is designed with broader sensibilities in mind than hard balancing everyone for combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. There are still a few issues with character gen, but much less than 2nd ed. There are easier ways to deal with it. Also, I think it encourages players to think that it's really important to be good at combat, but a good ST can fit the combats to the PCs.<br /> In my 265xp game, half the characters don't have combat abilities at 5, and most of them don't have Dex 5. As I only have a combat every 3 sessions-ish, this works very well.<br /> Of course, if you're running a very high-combat game, I could see the value.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T04:32:45-08:00","id":763947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/763367-3e-homebrew-lightbringers-an-alternate-solar-creation-advancement-system-3e-update?p=763626#post763626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And finally, being honest, not sure what the exact problem with the Artifact requirement is? I always liked it for how it gave players fun toys right from the get go.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>If everyone has Artifact 5, it means that taking an Artifact is not a meaningful and personal choice of the character with an associated opportunity cost. Instead it's just something you do. In some ways it implies that you're not a proper Exalt if you lack them. The system changes to weapons still leave mortal weapons very viable; the biggest boon with armor is Hardness. <br /> <br /> And not everyone wants to have an Artifact. There's that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T06:19:24-08:00","id":763995,"title":"","content":"I don't think I've ever had a character with an Artefact at 5.<br /> My Dragonblood generally had a few low-level artefacts, my Celestials rarely have artefacts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T06:39:42-08:00","id":764006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/763367-3e-homebrew-lightbringers-an-alternate-solar-creation-advancement-system-3e-update?p=763995#post763995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I've ever had a character with an Artefact at 5.<br /> My Dragonblood generally had a few low-level artefacts, my Celestials rarely have artefacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably you could break that single 5 into smaller components?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T06:49:07-08:00","id":764011,"title":"","content":"Presumably, though I've never had a non-Dynast/Alchemical with 5 dots of artefacts total at character gen.<br /> Neither\u200b did any of the PCs in the game I run at character gen... though once there was a guy with a Daiklaive of Conquest (he doesn't play anymore).<br /> Most of them started with 2-dots of Artefact.<br /> One Lunar has two daiklaives she took off enemies nowadays though, so she has 6 dots (as those are now 3-dot).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T06:54:53-08:00","id":764017,"title":"","content":"Saying this, I do think it solves what I assume what Side Item wants, which is providing every character with similar combat stats, since pretty much all of them will have a magic weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T10:27:32-08:00","id":764182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Root</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/763367-3e-homebrew-lightbringers-an-alternate-solar-creation-advancement-system-3e-update?p=763819#post763819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue with this for new players is that, while no one will have an ineffective character, character creation is a lot more intimidating in a way that could carry over into the game. It sends the message that 5s are necessary because the system is so brittle and because organic choices will ruin your character. Lightbringers helped in 2e, where it really did protect people from a lot of bad surprises.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want to make a player think, &quot;Oh shit, I've only got 7 dice in Charisma + Presence. I should shut up and let the good characters handle this,&quot; or &quot;My score isn't 5 in this ability, so picking up charms is a waste.&quot; Of course you can communicate to your players that they don't need huge dice pools to succeed or to invest in an area, but anyone willing to say that probably wouldn't use this system...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I can see where you're coming from. I'm not entirely convinced though where the 'intimidation' comes from? Again, I see it as a benefit of the system that the choices are constrained/not organic. If that's what you wanted you'd go with the RAW.<br /> <br /> In regards to the &quot;Well, I'm not tall enough to contribute&quot; thing, I loved playing with the system because you were always tall enough in some way to contribute at all times. Sure, you might not have picked Presence 5, but you did pick Socialize or Integrity and can contribute that way. The situations where you have absolutely no way to be proactive should be exceedingly rare under this system, and if I've missed some way where those situations pop up let me know.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If everyone has Artifact 5, it means that taking an Artifact is not a meaningful and personal choice of the character with an associated opportunity cost. Instead it's just something you do. In some ways it implies that you're not a proper Exalt if you lack them. The system changes to weapons still leave mortal weapons very viable; the biggest boon with armor is Hardness. <br /> <br /> And not everyone wants to have an Artifact. There's that too. </div> </div> </div>True. I suppose it couldn't hurt to add the &quot;If a character doesn't use Artifacts they should negotiate for a suitable replacement&quot; from the advancement section to the chargen section.<br /> <br /> And reading the other discussion...is the issue the five dots of Artifacts, or a single five dot Artifact? Because it says that at chargen you can't get something higher than 3 dots. Weapon and Armor is the norm I usually saw, but miscellaneous utility artifacts wasn't unheard of.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T11:19:03-08:00","id":764224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/763367-3e-homebrew-lightbringers-an-alternate-solar-creation-advancement-system-3e-update?p=764182#post764182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I can see where you're coming from. I'm not entirely convinced though where the 'intimidation' comes from? Again, I see it as a benefit of the system that the choices are constrained/not organic. If that's what you wanted you'd go with the RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some players would be intimidated because they would infer that scores less than 5 are bad. They'd definitely have strengths, but wouldn't feel as comfortable using anything that wasn't maxed out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/763367-3e-homebrew-lightbringers-an-alternate-solar-creation-advancement-system-3e-update?p=764182#post764182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the &quot;Well, I'm not tall enough to contribute&quot; thing, I loved playing with the system because you were always tall enough in some way to contribute at all times. Sure, you might not have picked Presence 5, but you did pick Socialize or Integrity and can contribute that way. The situations where you have absolutely no way to be proactive should be exceedingly rare under this system, and if I've missed some way where those situations pop up let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, so this is what I was talking about. Can't the Presence 3 character pick up a few charms and contribute? My experience says yes, but maybe we're talking about very different challenges here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}